  "documented_limitations": [
    "The owner collection tool refuses against the active guard 1.2.0, because that version has no qualification layer and the tool will not describe a guard in words it does not have. Every gate check uses the repository copy and states that source in its report. This resolves on activation.",
    "The recording of ignored objects begins on activation. Until then the observation area does not exist and recording is a no-op, which is the documented behaviour.",
    "mf-evidence and mf-phase-results aggregated an empty set during the acceptance run, because the evidence of this block is committed in the determinative commit that follows it. They are meaningful for a later re-run, not for this one.",
    "The R9 declaration covers the seven functions this block introduced or repaired. The corpus wide review is deferred to a separate test hardening step and is not claimed here.",
    "The product guard declaration is unchanged from B0c: allowed_paths is a single wildcard, because the examined range starts at the line origin and that range already touches product paths from before this line of work. The statement that this block changed no product code rests on the block delta, not on that declaration."
  ]
